    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_presenting_arguments_claim",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-presenting-arguments-01",
        "text": {
          "en": "I would state the claim early, then make clear which evidence supports it and which evidence merely provides context."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "ادعا رو زود مطرح می‌کنم و بعد روشن می‌کنم کدوم شواهد حمایتش می‌کنن و کدوم فقط زمینه می‌دن."
        },
        "intent": "structure_claim",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_presenting_arguments_claim",
          "c1_presenting_arguments_evidence"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "questions",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_presenting_arguments_premise",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-presenting-arguments-01",
        "text": {
          "en": "The argument depends on a premise the audience may not share, so I would surface it before moving to the conclusion."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "استدلال به پیش‌فرضی وابسته‌ست که شاید مخاطب قبولش نداشته باشه، پس قبل از نتیجه صریحش می‌کنم."
        },
        "intent": "surface_premise",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_presenting_arguments_argument",
          "c1_presenting_arguments_premise"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "questions",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_presenting_arguments_sequence",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-presenting-arguments-02",
        "text": {
          "en": "The sequence matters: if the audience hears the recommendation before the problem is established, the proposal can feel predetermined."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "توالی مهمه؛ اگر مخاطب قبل از روشن شدن مشکل توصیه رو بشنوه، پیشنهاد ممکنه از قبل تصمیم‌گرفته‌شده به نظر بیاد."
        },
        "intent": "sequence_argument",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_presenting_arguments_sequence",
          "c1_presenting_arguments_claim"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "questions",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_presenting_arguments_signpost",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-presenting-arguments-02",
        "text": {
          "en": "I would signpost the shift from evidence to interpretation so the audience can see where judgment enters the argument."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "تغییر از شواهد به تفسیر رو علامت‌گذاری می‌کنم تا مخاطب ببینه قضاوت کجا وارد استدلال می‌شه."
        },
        "intent": "signpost_reasoning",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_presenting_arguments_signpost",
          "c1_presenting_arguments_evidence"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "questions",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_presenting_arguments_rebuttal",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-presenting-arguments-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "A rebuttal is strongest when it addresses the best version of the opposing argument rather than an easy caricature."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "پاسخ مخالف وقتی قوی‌تره که به بهترین نسخه استدلال طرف مقابل جواب بده، نه یک کاریکاتور ساده‌شده."
        },
        "intent": "build_rebuttal",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_presenting_arguments_rebuttal",
          "c1_presenting_arguments_argument"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "questions",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_presenting_arguments_implication",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-presenting-arguments-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "After each major point, I would make the practical implication explicit instead of assuming the audience will infer it."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "بعد از هر نکته اصلی پیامد عملی رو صریح می‌کنم، به‌جای اینکه فرض کنم مخاطب خودش استنباطش می‌کنه."
        },
        "intent": "state_implication",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_presenting_arguments_implication",
          "c1_presenting_arguments_signpost"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "questions",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_presenting_arguments_limit",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-presenting-arguments-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "The conclusion should be no broader than the evidence allows; otherwise a strong argument can be weakened by an overstated ending."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "نتیجه نباید از چیزی که شواهد اجازه می‌دن گسترده‌تر باشه؛ وگرنه پایان اغراق‌آمیز یک استدلال قوی رو ضعیف می‌کنه."
        },
        "intent": "calibrate_conclusion",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_presenting_arguments_evidence",
          "c1_presenting_arguments_claim"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "questions",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_presenting_arguments_close",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-presenting-arguments-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "To close, I would restate the claim in light of the evidence rather than simply repeating the opening sentence."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "در پایان ادعا رو با توجه به شواهد دوباره بیان می‌کنم، نه اینکه فقط جمله اول رو تکرار کنم."
        },
        "intent": "close_argument",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_presenting_arguments_claim",
          "c1_presenting_arguments_evidence"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "questions",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_presenting_arguments_discourse_management",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-presenting-arguments-01",
        "slug": "c1-presenting-arguments-discourse-management",
        "title": "Managing complex discourse",
        "rule_summary": "Use signposting and metadiscourse to frame, sequence, return to, and close complex points without losing the listener.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "با signposting و metadiscourse نکات پیچیده را قاب‌بندی، مرتب، دوباره جمع و نتیجه‌گیری می‌کنیم تا شنونده مسیر بحث را گم نکند."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "Before I come back to that point, let me clarify one assumption.",
            "fa": "قبل از اینکه به آن نکته برگردم، بگذار یک فرض را روشن کنم."
          },
          {
            "en": "That brings us to the broader question of accountability.",
            "fa": "این ما را به پرسش گسترده‌تر پاسخ‌گویی می‌رساند."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_presenting_arguments_rhetorical_questions",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-presenting-arguments-02",
        "slug": "c1-presenting-arguments-rhetorical-questions",
        "title": "Rhetorical questions in argument",
        "rule_summary": "Use rhetorical questions sparingly to foreground an implication, then answer or develop the point rather than leaving it vague.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "از سؤال بلاغی با احتیاط برای برجسته کردن یک پیامد استفاده می‌کنیم و بعد پاسخ یا استدلال را ادامه می‌دهیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "If the data are incomplete, how confident can we really be?",
            "fa": "اگر داده‌ها ناقص‌اند، واقعاً چقدر می‌توانیم مطمئن باشیم؟"
          },
          {
            "en": "What happens when the exception becomes the norm?",
            "fa": "وقتی استثنا تبدیل به قاعده شود چه اتفاقی می‌افتد؟"
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_presenting_arguments_cleft_sentences",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-presenting-arguments-03",
        "slug": "c1-presenting-arguments-cleft-sentences",
        "title": "Cleft sentences for focus",
        "rule_summary": "Use what-clauses and it-clefts to place deliberate emphasis on the most important part of a message.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "با what-clause و it-cleft بخش مهم پیام را برجسته می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "What concerns me most is the lack of independent oversight.",
            "fa": "چیزی که بیشتر نگرانم می‌کند نبود نظارت مستقل است."
          },
          {
            "en": "It was the timing, rather than the decision itself, that caused the problem.",
            "fa": "زمان‌بندی بود، نه خود تصمیم، که مشکل را ایجاد کرد."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "external_id": "d_c1_presenting_arguments_scene_1",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-presenting-arguments-01",
        "title": "Presenting Arguments: part 1",
        "setting": "strategy meeting",
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "questions",
        "characters": [
          "Noor",
          "Liam"
        ],
        "turns": [
          {
            "order": 1,
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "What do you make of the way this is being framed?",
            "translation_fa": "از نحوه مطرح شدن این موضوع چه برداشتی داری؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 2,
            "speaker": "Liam",
            "text": "I would state the claim early, then make clear which evidence supports it and which evidence merely provides context.",
            "translation_fa": "ادعا رو زود مطرح می‌کنم و بعد روشن می‌کنم کدوم شواهد حمایتش می‌کنن و کدوم فقط زمینه می‌دن."
          },
          {
            "order": 3,
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Is there another interpretation we should keep in view?",
            "translation_fa": "تفسیر دیگه‌ای هست که باید در نظر داشته باشیم؟"
          },
